package runner

const replanRules = "## Rules (replan mode)\nThe plan drifted from reality. Fix the plan, not the code: the Replan mode\nof the `bsv-docflow-plan` skill if you have it; the rules below are\ncomplete without it.\n1. Read the trigger, the Handoffs of the done units (a moved file's new\n   path is usually there) and `## Decisions`.\n2. Edit only the plan file: units `[ ]` and `[!]`, new units with the next\n   numbers of the phase, Context links, Traps; append to Decisions. Do not\n   renumber the existing units: Depends and commits refer to them.\n3. Never change the frontmatter, Goal, Constraints or Prerequisites, and\n   never change or delete a `[x]` or `[-]` unit: they are history. An\n   existing unit id never disappears. `Verify:`, `Do:` and `Role:` of a unit\nwith `Role: review` or `Role: acceptance` stay as they are and such a unit\nnever moves to `[-]`: they are the reference checks of the plan, the guard\nagainst weakening the check of one's own work; only the status marker and\n`Depends:` of those units change.\n4. Every `Read:` and Context link of the open units must point to a file\n   that exists now.\n5. Lift the block of a `[!]` unit: `[~]` when the uncommitted work listed\n   under \"Tree\" still stands after your edit (a `[~]` unit resumes on\n   it); `[ ]` when the tree is clean; `[-]` when new units replace it.\n   Uncommitted work that is no longer needed: reply blocked, never roll it\n   back. A unit refused by `prompt` for a stale link stays `[ ]`.\n6. Do not do the unit's work and do not touch any other file; uncommitted\n   work in the tree stays as it is.\n7. Run `docflow lint` and fix every error and every \"file not found\".\n8. Do not commit.\n9. End your reply with the result JSON as the last ```json block, every\n   key present (an empty list or string when unused):\n   {\"status\": \"done\", \"handoff\": [\"...\"], \"decisions\": [],\n    \"unverified\": [], \"reason\": \"\", \"blocker\": \"\"}\n   - handoff: what you changed in the plan and why, one item per change.\n   When the plan cannot be fixed without the user, reply\n   {\"status\": \"blocked\", \"handoff\": [], \"decisions\": [],\n    \"unverified\": [], \"reason\": \"<what exactly the user must do>\",\n    \"blocker\": \"human\"}.\n"
